WEBVTT

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:04.580
Good morning!

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:06.020
It's time to wake up!

00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:13.530
Io-chin, you're all disheveled again.

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:16.280
Hurry up and go wash your face.

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:21.410
Good morning!

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:24.080
Hi there, Boss! Did you eat your food?

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:26.080
What? You're not hungry today?

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:30.130
Time to eat!

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.380
Hey, by the way,

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:38.010
did you hear the rumor about the 
physics teacher that came last week?

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:39.150
Rumor?

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:39.760
Yeah.

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:41.430
She came in a week ago.

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:43.770
She's got a mysterious aura about her.

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:47.220
She seems kind of... airy.

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:50.760
Your explanation seems 
like nothing but air, too.

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:55.650
Yeah, so there's this rumor that 
says she's not from this world!

00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:57.360
What?! Really?

00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:59.010
What's that about?

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:00.380
Why would people say that?

00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:02.820
Well, if you're really good at physics,

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:05.620
you could probably easily 
float into space, I bet.

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:07.450
What? Really?

00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:10.240
So that's what "airy" means!

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:11.770
Wow!

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:14.020
That can't be it.

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:15.620
What? She was lying?

00:01:17.870 --> 00:01:23.640
Maybe that mysterious aura about her 
has something to do with the O'bli?

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:25.550
Oh, <i>nyow</i> I get it.

00:01:25.550 --> 00:01:28.300
Tsubame-chan, you're such a diligent girl,

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:30.880
thinking about your mission even here, meow.

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:35.360
But this is when you need that beautiful 
girl detective everyone's talking about.

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:38.240
I bet she'd be able to figure out who 
that girl really is in an instant.

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:41.300
Beautiful girl detective?

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:42.160
Yeah.

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:43.860
She's a student at our school,

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:47.140
and she's helped solve tons 
of mysteries at the school.

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:49.060
She's a great detective.

00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:50.350
This is a rumor, too.

00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:52.750
Oh, I've heard about her, too.

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:59.180
I guess school mysteries really are 
vital to a healthy student lifestyle.

00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:01.460
A beautiful detective, huh?

00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:04.680
If she exists, I wonder if she'd 
help us research the O'bli.

00:02:06.330 --> 00:02:07.890
Tsubame is so serious, meow.

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:10.160
Not you too, Io!

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:47.760
<b>Arrived! The Beautiful Detective Everyone's Talking About</b>

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:50.090
Hey, Io-chin.

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:55.750
Everyone's saying the pancake shop that 
opened up the other day is really good,

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:57.180
so let's go!

00:03:57.180 --> 00:04:00.940
Sorry, the Red and White 
Tournament is coming up.

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:03.240
I have to show up at practice.

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:04.430
Aww!

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:07.560
But it sounds good,

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:09.980
so let me know how it is later.

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:15.080
She turned me down.

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:16.940
I'm so shocked.

00:04:18.220 --> 00:04:21.200
Mana-chan, I'll go with you, if you want.

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:22.340
Really?

00:04:22.340 --> 00:04:24.180
Thanks, Yuumi-chin!

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:25.510
What about you, Satoka-chan?

00:04:25.510 --> 00:04:27.760
You'll come and have some pancakes, right?

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:30.520
I have work today.

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:32.920
Huh? Sato-chin, you have a part-time job?

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:34.500
I didn't know that, either.

00:04:37.180 --> 00:04:39.510
Anyway, I'll be taking my leave.

00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:49.260
Tell me how the pancakes are.

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:49.970
In detail.

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:52.980
Oh, sure. No problem.

00:04:57.510 --> 00:05:00.380
I wonder what job Sato-chin has.

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:01.660
Oh, well.

00:05:01.660 --> 00:05:02.750
Let's go, just us two.

00:05:02.750 --> 00:05:03.570
Yeah!

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:06.910
In detail.

00:05:06.910 --> 00:05:09.050
W-We got it! We got it!

00:05:09.050 --> 00:05:10.950
I'll make the same one for you later!

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:13.480
Thank you.

00:05:15.670 --> 00:05:18.830
Sato-chin really wants 
to go eat with us, huh?

00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:21.780
Hee-hee.

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:24.180
There've been a lot of weird rumors lately.

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:26.180
If I make a special on them 
for the school paper,

00:05:26.180 --> 00:05:27.840
we'll get more copies out there...

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:28.430
Mountain.

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:31.200
Oh, Satokacchi!

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:32.460
I've been waiting for you.

00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:35.230
So what did you need, Ako-san?

00:05:35.230 --> 00:05:38.820
Well, a lot's been happening lately, right?

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:39.690
I guess?

00:05:39.690 --> 00:05:45.440
I was surprised that you got 
chosen for the Fifth Force, too.

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:48.350
I kind of figured it'd happen someday, though.

00:05:48.350 --> 00:05:50.890
You can stop being patronizing.

00:05:50.890 --> 00:05:54.920
We have a strictly business relationship.

00:05:54.920 --> 00:05:57.040
We're B2B, a win-win.

00:05:58.500 --> 00:06:01.630
By the way, I still haven't heard 
your answer to the pass phrase.

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:04.030
Maybe you're not the real Ako-san...

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:06.010
So how's Altair Torte?

00:06:07.940 --> 00:06:11.650
Well, I think we have a promising future.

00:06:11.650 --> 00:06:14.890
I guess if I were to put it 
in terms of a marathon,

00:06:14.890 --> 00:06:18.740
we're finally approaching 
the next task, I suppose.

00:06:18.740 --> 00:06:20.770
What do tasks have to do with a marathon?

00:06:27.450 --> 00:06:30.360
A member of the Fifth Force is being stalked?

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:33.460
Well, we're not sure yet.

00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:37.160
It's Shinonome Ryoukocchi of 
my team, Coconut Vega.

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:38.880
Shinonome...

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:40.790
Oh, yeah.

00:06:41.020 --> 00:06:45.800
She said she feels like someone's 
been watching her lately.

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:47.960
Feels like someone's watching her?

00:06:47.960 --> 00:06:51.340
She feels creeped out because 
no one's there when she looks around.

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:54.470
That would be unsettling.

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:58.520
And I'm currently seeing if there are any 
similar rumors going around the school.

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:00.060
I see.

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:02.570
Anyway, thanks for your help with that.

00:07:02.570 --> 00:07:04.210
The next thing I have...

00:07:04.210 --> 00:07:06.180
You have more?

00:07:06.180 --> 00:07:10.110
I haven't been able to ask you anything 
for a while, so they've been piling up.

00:07:14.040 --> 00:07:16.870
That means they're lying.

00:07:16.870 --> 00:07:18.620
It was raining that day,

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:20.990
so the route to school would 
have been different.

00:07:20.990 --> 00:07:23.540
It's difficult to think they 
would have met up there.

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:27.850
It makes more sense that they 
secretly met before that.

00:07:27.850 --> 00:07:29.170
I get it!

00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:31.470
That's some great deductive ability.

00:07:32.920 --> 00:07:34.600
Nice going, Satokacchi.

00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:36.640
We got through all these in no time.

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:40.740
I can tell you've been secretly working 
at a detective agency part-time.

00:07:40.740 --> 00:07:43.600
It's not like I'm trying to hide it.

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:46.990
People are talking about you, you know.

00:07:46.990 --> 00:07:50.460
Who would have thought the 
beautiful detective was you, huh?

00:07:50.460 --> 00:07:51.200
Hee-hee.

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:54.140
I wish you'd stop calling me that.

00:07:54.140 --> 00:07:56.620
Aww, you really don't mind it at all, do you?

00:07:57.000 --> 00:07:58.790
I'm just an assistant.

00:07:58.790 --> 00:08:01.460
I can't go around saying I'm a detective.

00:08:01.720 --> 00:08:02.880
<i>That's</i> the problem?

00:08:04.520 --> 00:08:06.290
You're okay with the beautiful part?

00:08:06.290 --> 00:08:09.060
Well, that's subjective, so it's your call.

00:08:09.060 --> 00:08:12.330
You've really got some nerve...

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:13.630
Huh?

00:08:15.150 --> 00:08:16.390
What's wrong?

00:08:25.940 --> 00:08:29.650
Oh, I see. So this is where it leads!

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:33.610
See? My idea wasn't wrong.

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:36.490
Yes, Lady Niho. You're always right.

00:08:36.490 --> 00:08:39.000
That's Hinomiya Nihocchi.

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:40.700
Why is she sneaking around?

00:08:42.510 --> 00:08:44.260
Hinomiya Niho...

00:08:45.070 --> 00:08:46.300
Who is she?

00:08:46.300 --> 00:08:47.230
What?

00:08:47.230 --> 00:08:48.980
You don't know?

00:08:48.980 --> 00:08:49.840
Nope.

00:08:50.100 --> 00:08:52.220
She's the heir to the 
Hinomiya Conglomerate.

00:08:52.220 --> 00:08:56.090
She's really famous and has done a lot 
at this school. You didn't know?

00:08:57.720 --> 00:09:02.220
I guess it'd be faster for me to say 
she's the leader of Biscuit Sirius.

00:09:02.220 --> 00:09:04.940
Oh, okay.

00:09:05.220 --> 00:09:06.310
Uh...

00:09:06.310 --> 00:09:09.180
It's amazing you can work 
at a detective agency when

00:09:09.180 --> 00:09:11.230
you can barely remember 
people's names and faces.

00:09:11.600 --> 00:09:15.120
All girls wearing uniforms 
look the same to me.

00:09:15.120 --> 00:09:15.650
What?

00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:19.570
When I raise the transmission 
efficiency of my synapses,

00:09:19.570 --> 00:09:22.300
which connect the neurons in my brain 
responsible for storing long-term memories,

00:09:22.300 --> 00:09:24.600
the hunger center in my 
hypothalamus gets stimulated,

00:09:24.600 --> 00:09:25.910
and I get hungry.

00:09:25.910 --> 00:09:27.280
So that's really unavoidable.

00:09:27.280 --> 00:09:28.510
I don't think so...

00:09:28.510 --> 00:09:33.510
Well, there isn't really a problem because 
you always tell me what I need to know.

00:09:35.270 --> 00:09:42.510
You know, Biscuit Sirius has the best results 
in Fifth Force. They're the strongest.

00:09:43.020 --> 00:09:45.050
Of course they've got strong 
combative abilities,

00:09:45.050 --> 00:09:47.230
but Hinomiya Nihocchi, their leader,

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:51.020
has her subordinates, twin sisters, 
Haishima Isari and Kagari...

00:09:51.420 --> 00:09:53.650
her childhood friend, Aoi Yukie...

00:09:53.980 --> 00:09:56.650
and her relative and lookout, Yamabuki Kaede.

00:09:56.900 --> 00:09:58.950
The teamwork between the five is amazing,

00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:01.090
and no one can keep up with them.

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:06.700
Honestly speaking, our Coconut Vega 
doesn't even come close to them.

00:10:07.080 --> 00:10:10.790
Ah. They were so far over our 
heads that I didn't notice them.

00:10:11.960 --> 00:10:14.680
I know a novice like me shouldn't say this, but...

00:10:16.210 --> 00:10:19.300
They don't really seem like the strongest.

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:21.430
Well, they normally are.

00:10:21.840 --> 00:10:24.430
Hmm? What's going on?

00:10:24.710 --> 00:10:30.620
So that weird moaning sound was just sounds 
from outside coming in through the duct.

00:10:30.620 --> 00:10:33.570
I guess we took care of this mystery, too.

00:10:33.830 --> 00:10:38.950
When you put your mind to something, 
Lady Niho, there's nothing you can't solve.

00:10:40.990 --> 00:10:42.240
What's wrong?

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:43.080
Nothing.

00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:44.670
Just our imaginations.

00:10:44.670 --> 00:10:45.580
I see.

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:48.450
So, Kaede, what's the next mystery?

00:10:48.450 --> 00:10:54.320
Supposedly there's a girl secretly 
acting as a detective at our school.

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:55.920
What's that about?

00:10:55.920 --> 00:10:58.610
That'd be pretty cool!

00:10:58.610 --> 00:11:01.550
That sounds interesting! Let's go!

00:11:02.500 --> 00:11:07.240
It looks like they're solving the 
mysteries and rumors at the school.

00:11:07.240 --> 00:11:09.600
And that's the legacy she's 
leaving here at school...

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:12.460
Nihocchi has a lot of curiosity.

00:11:12.460 --> 00:11:13.440
I see.

00:11:14.120 --> 00:11:16.420
Oh, hey, Satokacchi...

00:11:16.840 --> 00:11:17.320
Yes?

00:11:17.910 --> 00:11:20.740
You know Altair Torte's leader?

00:11:20.740 --> 00:11:22.260
You mean Tsubame-san?

00:11:22.260 --> 00:11:24.290
They say she doesn't have any memories.

00:11:24.290 --> 00:11:25.700
Just who is she?

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:28.910
You don't know either, Ako-san?

00:11:29.340 --> 00:11:33.790
I still don't have any idea where 
Tsubame-san came from, either.

00:11:34.820 --> 00:11:36.210
Hey!

00:11:37.620 --> 00:11:39.770
Where did you go?

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:54.620
Hey, Yuumi-chin?

00:11:54.620 --> 00:11:55.310
Yes?

00:11:55.310 --> 00:11:59.470
Those pancakes everyone was 
talking about weren't that good.

00:11:59.470 --> 00:12:03.030
It only looked really nice, 
and it was really expensive.

00:12:03.260 --> 00:12:05.220
You sure tell it how it is, Mana-chan.

00:12:05.220 --> 00:12:07.450
But there were some good things.

00:12:07.720 --> 00:12:11.410
If Io-chin had been with us, 
she would have been disappointed.

00:12:11.770 --> 00:12:13.410
That was close.

00:12:13.410 --> 00:12:16.790
I guess you can't just 
blindly believe every rumor.

00:12:19.360 --> 00:12:21.970
Yuumi-chin, what's wrong?

00:12:22.940 --> 00:12:26.340
Wait, did you think those pancakes were good?

00:12:27.500 --> 00:12:30.660
I hurt Yuumi-chin!

00:12:30.660 --> 00:12:33.040
I-It's okay, Mana-chan.

00:12:33.040 --> 00:12:35.150
The pancakes really weren't that good.

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:36.650
Really?

00:12:36.650 --> 00:12:38.520
Thank goodness! They weren't, right?

00:12:38.780 --> 00:12:39.700
Yeah.

00:12:41.020 --> 00:12:44.990
I felt like someone was watching me just now.

00:12:44.990 --> 00:12:45.990
Huh?

00:12:45.990 --> 00:12:47.730
That's scary.

00:12:47.730 --> 00:12:50.760
But I think I was just imagining it.

00:12:50.760 --> 00:12:52.380
No one's here.

00:12:52.380 --> 00:12:53.250
Er, Mana-chan?

00:12:53.640 --> 00:12:59.840
To be honest, I feel like someone's 
watching me when no one's around, too.

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:01.280
Huh? Really?

00:13:01.280 --> 00:13:02.460
Sometimes.

00:13:02.460 --> 00:13:05.990
Like someone's checking on me.

00:13:05.990 --> 00:13:07.450
Checking on you?

00:13:07.450 --> 00:13:10.010
That's kind of how it felt for me, too.

00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:12.680
How scary!

00:13:19.600 --> 00:13:20.360
Listen!

00:13:20.730 --> 00:13:22.360
Everyone listen!

00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:24.950
Wow.

00:13:27.900 --> 00:13:29.410
Don't say "wow"!

00:13:29.410 --> 00:13:30.410
Dummy!

00:13:30.410 --> 00:13:32.450
Yuumi, where've you been?

00:13:32.820 --> 00:13:33.760
Oh, yeah!

00:13:33.760 --> 00:13:37.620
There are others who have felt 
someone watching them!

00:13:38.020 --> 00:13:43.790
You mean the thing Mana said, 
like someone was checking on her?

00:13:43.790 --> 00:13:46.090
It wasn't just us?

00:13:46.090 --> 00:13:46.760
Yeah.

00:13:47.470 --> 00:13:49.380
Ryouko-chan said the same thing,

00:13:49.380 --> 00:13:52.640
and Kyoubashi Amane-chan
from Procyon Pudding.

00:13:52.640 --> 00:13:57.880
Also, Isari-chan and Kagari-chan 
from Biscuit Sirius.

00:13:57.880 --> 00:13:59.040
They all said they felt it.

00:13:59.040 --> 00:14:00.310
That many?!

00:14:02.130 --> 00:14:05.440
A case where people are 
being checked on by someone...

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:07.150
The "checking case."

00:14:07.150 --> 00:14:09.520
And it wasn't just one or two times.

00:14:09.520 --> 00:14:12.410
It's happened a lot lately.

00:14:12.850 --> 00:14:14.010
I see...

00:14:14.010 --> 00:14:15.950
A serial checking case.

00:14:16.350 --> 00:14:18.850
And it isn't just when someone's outside.

00:14:18.850 --> 00:14:21.590
It happens in locked rooms, too.

00:14:22.850 --> 00:14:24.920
A locked room checking case.

00:14:25.170 --> 00:14:28.660
Everyone's talking about it, even in Eterno.

00:14:28.660 --> 00:14:32.330
With that many people, you can't just 
chalk it up to everyone's imaginations.

00:14:32.330 --> 00:14:34.640
Maybe we should look into it.

00:14:35.210 --> 00:14:37.690
But how?

00:14:39.260 --> 00:14:40.510
I know!

00:14:40.510 --> 00:14:43.520
We can ask the beautiful 
detective-chin to help!

00:14:43.830 --> 00:14:48.280
Mana-chan, didn't you just learn not 
to believe every rumor you hear?

00:14:48.550 --> 00:14:52.030
And we don't know if she really exists.

00:14:55.670 --> 00:14:57.920
You control rumors with rumors!

00:14:57.920 --> 00:15:01.630
Tell me more about this checking thing!

00:15:02.240 --> 00:15:03.840
Wow.

00:15:08.060 --> 00:15:10.420
All the people who have 
experienced the checking

00:15:10.420 --> 00:15:12.300
are members of the Fifth Force.

00:15:12.590 --> 00:15:16.720
These are all the locations where 
it's happened in the last week.

00:15:17.120 --> 00:15:21.270
<i>There doesn't seem to be any relationship 
with the previous locations</i>

00:15:21.270 --> 00:15:23.280
<i>of distortions in space-time.</i>

00:15:23.730 --> 00:15:24.690
<i>That means...</i>

00:15:24.690 --> 00:15:26.190
I finally found you.

00:15:27.500 --> 00:15:31.680
Oh, you're, um... the Biscuit Sirius leader...

00:15:31.680 --> 00:15:33.320
Hinomiya Niho.

00:15:33.320 --> 00:15:36.520
I wouldn't have expected you, 
a member of Altair Torte,

00:15:36.520 --> 00:15:38.120
to be the rumored beautiful detective!

00:15:38.800 --> 00:15:40.620
Uh...

00:15:41.100 --> 00:15:42.980
Huh? Was I wrong?

00:15:42.980 --> 00:15:46.210
No, you're probably right, but...

00:15:46.210 --> 00:15:47.200
But?

00:15:47.200 --> 00:15:49.380
I would like to correct part of that.

00:15:51.980 --> 00:15:53.260
I see.

00:15:53.560 --> 00:15:55.570
So you're working in the detective field,

00:15:55.570 --> 00:15:57.890
but you're not a proper detective in name.

00:15:58.320 --> 00:15:59.530
That's right.

00:15:59.530 --> 00:16:03.100
So it's difficult for me to respond when 
people call me a beautiful detective.

00:16:03.300 --> 00:16:04.880
I see. Sorry about that.

00:16:04.880 --> 00:16:05.700
In that case...

00:16:05.700 --> 00:16:06.960
Hey there, beautiful!

00:16:06.960 --> 00:16:08.940
I see. So that's where you went.

00:16:08.940 --> 00:16:11.290
That's pretty difficult to respond to, too.

00:16:11.290 --> 00:16:12.760
You're a real pain.

00:16:12.760 --> 00:16:15.170
It doesn't matter what I call you.

00:16:15.170 --> 00:16:16.490
Yeah, that's true.

00:16:16.720 --> 00:16:21.400
Anyway, I'd like to ask you something, 
since you do detective stuff.

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:25.850
Could it be looking into 
the serial checking case?

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:27.130
What's that?

00:16:27.460 --> 00:16:30.750
Well, Isari-san and Kagari-san are worried

00:16:30.750 --> 00:16:33.340
about feeling someone watching them, right?

00:16:34.700 --> 00:16:36.170
Looks like I'm right.

00:16:36.700 --> 00:16:39.810
I'd like to ask you two about that.

00:16:43.110 --> 00:16:44.280
I see.

00:16:44.280 --> 00:16:46.400
That's some useful information.

00:16:46.400 --> 00:16:48.100
Did you figure something out?

00:16:48.100 --> 00:16:49.420
Well, yes.

00:16:51.320 --> 00:16:52.530
The culprit is probably...

00:16:57.450 --> 00:16:59.910
Oh, Satoka. Have you seen Boss?

00:17:00.600 --> 00:17:02.010
About that...

00:17:02.910 --> 00:17:05.580
<i>We've received an emergency SOS, moshu!</i>

00:17:05.860 --> 00:17:09.700
<i>Io-chan and Yuumi-chan have 
encountered a large O'bli at Point S.</i>

00:17:09.700 --> 00:17:12.730
<i>Any members on standby are 
to provide backup, moshu.</i>

00:17:12.730 --> 00:17:13.910
Oh, no!

00:17:15.660 --> 00:17:17.130
We need to go, too.

00:17:25.360 --> 00:17:26.600
What is this thing?

00:17:26.950 --> 00:17:28.530
It's so big.

00:17:28.810 --> 00:17:31.380
No! I can't handle this!

00:17:31.380 --> 00:17:32.650
Everyone, calm down.

00:17:34.450 --> 00:17:35.400
That's it?

00:17:35.990 --> 00:17:38.280
You don't mind us taking your prey, right?

00:18:03.970 --> 00:18:06.730
I won't let you lay one finger on Lady Niho!

00:18:08.650 --> 00:18:10.400
Eliminating the target.

00:18:18.390 --> 00:18:20.580
What? It was just one?

00:18:20.580 --> 00:18:21.780
It looks that way.

00:18:21.780 --> 00:18:24.890
There was no need for you to
trouble yourself with this.

00:18:24.890 --> 00:18:28.920
Aw, man! I didn't get to kick it enough!

00:18:29.370 --> 00:18:30.500
Wow.

00:18:30.990 --> 00:18:33.680
So that's Biscuit Sirius.

00:18:33.680 --> 00:18:36.170
No wonder they're called the strongest team.

00:18:36.170 --> 00:18:38.380
Niho-chan, that was amazing! Thanks!

00:18:39.030 --> 00:18:40.510
Y-Yeah, I guess.

00:18:41.280 --> 00:18:42.980
Wait, where's Satoka?

00:18:45.030 --> 00:18:46.220
Boss!

00:18:46.580 --> 00:18:48.280
You were in here?

00:18:48.280 --> 00:18:49.810
Yes, and...

00:18:50.410 --> 00:18:53.190
This is the culprit in the 
serial checking incident.

00:18:53.640 --> 00:18:54.840
What?!

00:18:56.740 --> 00:19:00.910
So this Boss cat went into the boundary

00:19:01.380 --> 00:19:05.090
and was watching all the members 
in the real world from there.

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:10.040
That's what was behind the checking incident.

00:19:10.310 --> 00:19:13.490
Oh, so it was just Boss watching me?

00:19:13.490 --> 00:19:15.410
That's not scary, then.

00:19:15.410 --> 00:19:18.370
So basically, anyone who took care of Boss,

00:19:18.370 --> 00:19:23.010
like Mana-san and Yuumi-san, 
were the ones affected.

00:19:23.210 --> 00:19:26.260
That's some special power you have.

00:19:26.580 --> 00:19:28.240
So you two, then...

00:19:28.240 --> 00:19:30.390
Yes, early yesterday morning,

00:19:30.390 --> 00:19:32.650
I was cleaning with Kagari...

00:19:32.650 --> 00:19:38.780
This Boss cat was there, so we gave him 
some food without a second thought.

00:19:39.020 --> 00:19:40.740
So that's what was going on.

00:19:41.090 --> 00:19:44.910
Boss, O'bli appear in the 
border, so it's dangerous.

00:19:44.910 --> 00:19:46.840
Try not to wander off there.

00:19:47.720 --> 00:19:50.900
Now that you mention it, he's a bit strange.

00:19:50.900 --> 00:19:53.060
I bet he's no ordinary cat.

00:19:53.060 --> 00:19:54.680
He's a beast, though.

00:19:55.620 --> 00:19:58.540
But why was he in the border?

00:19:58.540 --> 00:20:03.470
I think something caused the 
dimensional distortions to spread.

00:20:04.600 --> 00:20:07.310
We should report it to Sensei.

00:20:07.530 --> 00:20:10.060
Way to go, beautiful detective!

00:20:10.440 --> 00:20:11.290
Right.

00:20:11.740 --> 00:20:13.020
You mean Satoka-chan?!

00:20:13.310 --> 00:20:16.940
Combat ability isn't the only 
thing needed for our missions.

00:20:16.940 --> 00:20:22.110
I imagine all of your abilities
will greatly help us in the future.

00:20:22.540 --> 00:20:25.250
We're expecting a lot from you, Altair Torte.

00:20:25.250 --> 00:20:27.330
Thank you.

00:20:27.580 --> 00:20:29.730
We can't lose to them!

00:20:29.730 --> 00:20:31.170
Yes, my lady.

00:20:31.170 --> 00:20:33.460
We'll try even harder.

00:20:33.460 --> 00:20:36.830
I'm always prepared to abandon 
everything to get the job done!

00:20:37.670 --> 00:20:39.710
I don't want to push myself that hard, but...

00:20:40.940 --> 00:20:42.550
This'll be fun.

00:20:43.080 --> 00:20:48.010
Biscuit Sirius isn't going to 
hold back on the next one!

00:20:48.720 --> 00:20:49.760
What did she mean?

00:20:50.040 --> 00:20:52.270
Not hold back?

00:20:54.270 --> 00:20:56.190
Yuumi-chin, you're amazing!

00:20:56.540 --> 00:21:00.060
You've perfectly recreated that bland flavor!

00:21:00.060 --> 00:21:02.490
There's still more, so go ahead and eat.

00:21:02.800 --> 00:21:07.070
Yeah, this really is kind of...

00:21:07.070 --> 00:21:09.330
You didn't have to recreate this.

00:21:09.330 --> 00:21:10.920
Do you understand, Io-chin?

00:21:10.920 --> 00:21:12.890
Do you understand my sorrow?

00:21:12.890 --> 00:21:14.120
Yeah.

00:21:14.460 --> 00:21:16.060
It must have been tough for you.

00:21:17.450 --> 00:21:20.960
Sato-chin was pretty cool 
today, like a detective.

00:21:20.960 --> 00:21:22.640
Who'd have thought it'd be Satoka?

00:21:22.640 --> 00:21:24.340
That was a shock.

00:21:24.340 --> 00:21:26.560
So, I was thinking...

00:21:26.560 --> 00:21:31.140
Maybe... Sato-chin is 
the beautiful detective.

00:21:31.140 --> 00:21:33.200
What do you think? Am I good at deducing?

00:21:33.200 --> 00:21:35.700
So she didn't notice.

00:23:12.870 --> 00:23:18.240
<i>How is it that the Boss cat can 
easily enter the border now?</i>

00:23:18.240 --> 00:23:22.320
<i>What changed since last week?</i>

00:23:35.930 --> 00:23:40.940
<b>White Hot! Team Battle</b>

00:23:37.860 --> 00:23:40.400
"White Hot! Team Battle."
